const body = `<h1>3.2b — Boolean Logic: Combining Conditions in Practice</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Access Checker</h3>
        <p>Many programs check multiple conditions at once. Create a class called <code>AccessChecker</code> that decides whether a player can enter a restricted area.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Declare three variables:
                <ul>
                    <li><code>int playerLevel</code> — set to 5</li>
                    <li><code>boolean hasKey</code> — set to false</li>
                    <li><code>boolean isAdmin</code> — set to false</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Use <strong>&&</strong> to check: playerLevel >= 3 AND hasKey. Print "Access granted" or "Access denied".</li>
            <li>Now modify the condition using <strong>||</strong>: allow access if <em>either</em> the player has a key OR is an admin. Print the result.</li>
            <li>Add a third check using <strong>!</strong>: deny access if the player is NOT level 1 and NOT an admin. Print the result.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Truth Table Check</h3>
        <p>Before running: what output do you expect for level=1, no key, not admin? Trace through each of your three checks by hand. Run the program. Did it match your prediction?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Booleans &amp; if Statements</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Boolean Logic &amp; De Morgan</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
